senses.gloss:
कण् cl. 1. P. कणति, चकाण, कणिष्यति, अकणीत्, or अकाणीत्, कणिता, to become small;
to sound, cry, Dhātup. xiii, 6;
to go, approach, Dhātup. xix, 32 : cl. 10. P. काणयति, to wink, close the eye with the lids or lashes, Dhātup. xxx, 41 :
Caus. काणयति (aor. अचीकणत् and अचकाणत्, Pat. on Pāṇ. vii, 4, 3), to sigh, sound;
 [cf. √ चन् and √ क्वन्.]

कण्ठ् cl. 1. P. Ā. कण्ठति, -ते: cl. 10. P. कण्ठयति, to mourn;
to long for, desire (cf. 2. उत्-कण्ठ), Dhātup. viii, 11;
 xxxiv, 40.
